| MkEther - build the EtherRPCEm DCI4 network driver inside the guest.
|
| There is no RISC OS C toolchain on the host, so this module is built here
| with the Acorn DDE, the same way SharedClipboard is. See
| riscos-progs/EtherRPCEm/README.md on the host.
|
| Every tool's output goes to a log file. It must never come back through the
| command channel: a compiler's output will block it.
|
Set EtherBld$Dir <Obey$Dir>
Dir <EtherBld$Dir>
|
| Guarded, because System: only exists once !Boot has run, and an error in an
| Obey file abandons the rest of it, which looks exactly like a build failure.
IfThere System:Modules.DDEUtils Then RMEnsure DDEUtils 1.66 RMLoad System:Modules.DDEUtils
|
IfThere <EtherBld$Dir>.log Then Else CDir <EtherBld$Dir>.log
|
| The AutoSense file is compiled in as a C array, so it has to be converted
| before the module is compiled.
<EtherBld$Dir>.bin2c -t "const unsigned char" -n autosense_file AutoSense.EtherRPCEm c.AutoSense { > log.bin2c }
|
cmhg -d h.ModHdr cmhg.ModHdr -o o.ModHdr { > log.cmhg }
cc -IC: -zM -Wp -c -o o.Module c.Module { > log.cc }
objasm -NoCache -o o.errors s.errors { > log.errors }
objasm -NoCache -o o.intveneer s.intveneer { > log.veneer }
link -rmf -o EtherRPCEm o.Module o.errors o.intveneer o.ModHdr C:o.stubs { > log.link }
|
| Leave a marker the host can look for, so a build that fell over part way
| through is not mistaken for one that finished.
Echo done { > log.finished }
